essbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMOJIMA ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHOWA DENKO KK</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAITO, KAZUMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMOJIMA, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHOWA DENKO KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAITO KAZUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMOJIMA ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAITO, KAZUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMOJIMA, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A capacitor having large capacitance per unit weight and preferred LC characteristics is provided. The capacitor includes a dielectric material between two electrodes, and the dielectric material has a two-layer structure which includes a first layer whose main ingredient is niobium oxide, NbOx (X=2.5), and a second layer whose main ingredient is a compound of niobium oxides, NbOx (X=2.5) and NbOx (X=2.0). Both the first and second layers of the dielectric material contain 90% or more NbOx by weight. The molar ratio between NbOx (X=2.5) and NbOx (X=2.0) in the second layer is 1:4 to 4:1.  Preferably, the proportion of the first layer in the two-layer structure is 0.01 to 10% by volume. Preferably, one of the electrodes partly contains niobium nitride, which in particular is made by nitrogenation of sintered niobium.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un condensateur doté d'une grande capacité par unité de masse et de caractéristiques LC préférées. Ce condensateur comporte un matériau diélectrique disposé entre deux électrodes et présentant une structure bicouche comprenant une première couche dont le composant principal est de l'oxyde de niobium, NbOx (x = 2,5), et une seconde couche dont le composant principal est un composé d'oxydes de niobium, NbOx (x = 2,5) et NbOx (x = 2,0). Ces première et seconde couches de matériau diélectrique contiennent chacune 90 % en poids ou plus de NbOx. Le rapport molaire entre NbOx (x = 2,5) et NbOx (x = 2,0) dans la seconde couche est compris entre 1:4 et 4:1. De préférence, la proportion de la première couche dans la structure bicouche est comprise entre 0,01 et 10 % en volume. De préférence, une des électrodes contient en partie du nitrure de niobium, qui est obtenu notamment par transformation azotée du niobium fritté.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>